{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-harness-seam-001-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/TestCommandUiCensusOpsTests.cs", "line": 308, "method": "Find_CtrlVocabularyMirrorsTheDumpsOwnKindNames", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TestCommands/TestCommandUiFind.cs:81; drop a ctrl name from CtrlValues -> red on the 13-count only; changing GuiTreeModel.cs:468 KindName -> stays green", "what_it_asserts": "Every CtrlValues entry appears in ValidCtrlNames.Split(','), and CtrlValues.Length == 13.", "why_weak": "ValidCtrlNames is the comma-join of CtrlValues (TestCommandUiFind.cs:88), so the loop only re-splits its own source and reds on nothing but a separator or filter change. The mirror the name claims (GuiTreeAssembler.KindName, GuiTreeModel.cs:468) is never read, so a kind rename on either side stays green.", "proposed_action": "Assert CtrlValues equals GuiTreeAssembler.KindName projected over every GuiNodeKind value, so a rename on either side reds.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-harness-seam-001-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/TestCommandUiCensusOpsTests.cs", "line": 1042, "method": "PointerPoll_UsesTheSameToleranceTheReadBackDoes", "category": "T3", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TestCommands/TestCommandUiPointer.cs:235; widen the LandedWithinTolerance comparison -> red; sut=multi-line integration (ParsekTestCommandAddon.UiPointer.cs:227-234 is the claimed coupling)", "what_it_asserts": "LandedWithinTolerance accepts an offset of exactly ReadBackTolerancePx and rejects one half a pixel beyond.", "why_weak": "The name and comment assert that DecidePoll's landed argument is LandedWithinTolerance and cannot drift; the body never calls DecidePoll, so a caller that recomputed landed with a different epsilon leaves this green.", "proposed_action": "Rename to LandedWithinTolerance_BoundaryIsExactlyReadBackTolerancePx, or add a source/behavior cell over the applier's landed computation.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
